// error: what is passed for `f` of `Pool.use` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `seen`, an `Array[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Pool.use` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches `last`, a module-level `var`, which every thread would share; share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex` held in a `val`
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Pool.use` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `a`, a `Conn`, whose field `uses` is a `var`; make it a `val`
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Pool.lease` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches `kept`, a module-level value holding a `Buffer[Conn]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// A pool's resource is reached by one call at a time and by nothing outside the pool, so the body it
// is lent to may not reach mutable values from around it, store it where code outside reaches it, or
// hand it to a body lent another resource; a lease's body is held to the same.
import avin.threads.Pool

class Conn()
  var uses = 0

var last = 0
val kept = Buffer[Conn]()

main()
  val pool = Pool[Conn, string](() -> Ok(Conn()), maxSize = 2)
  val seen = Array.fill(3, 0)
  _ = pool.use(c -> seen(0) = c.uses)
  _ = pool.use(c -> last = c.uses)
  _ = pool.use(a -> pool.use(b -> a.uses + b.uses))
  _ = pool.lease(l -> kept.addOne(l.resource))
